NAME
     diff - compare two files line by line

SYNOPSIS
     diff [-u] [-c] [-q] [-s] [-i] [-w] [-b] [-B] [-N] [-r] [-U N] A B

DESCRIPTION
     diff prints the lines that would have to change to turn A into B.
     Either name may be a directory, with -r to compare what is in them,
     or - for standard input. The exit status is 0 when they are the
     same, 1 when they differ and 2 on an error, which is what makes it
     useful in a script.

OPTIONS
     -u      unified output (the usual form, with @@ hunk headers)
     -U N    unified, with N lines of context
     -c      context output
     -q      say only whether they differ
     -s      say so when they are identical
     -i      ignore case
     -w      ignore all whitespace
     -b      ignore changes in the amount of whitespace
     -B      ignore lines that are entirely blank
     -N      treat a missing file as empty
     -r      compare directories, and what is under them

SEE ALSO
     patch(1), cmp(1), comm(1)
